   794  ## Decisions
   795
   796  - **Merged Phase 7 & 8**: User confirmed they're the same work (physical control + alerting thresholds)
   797  - **Priority Order**: 1) Geist relay, 2) X410 (monitor + control), 3) Govee, 4) Grafana webhooks
   798  - **X410 Credentials**: User has IP/creds for online unit (will provide)
   799  - **Grafana Integration**: Option 1 (webhook from alert rules → Python script) - easiest native integration
   800  - **Webhook Receiver**: Separate Flask service (not part of Telegraf) for clean separation of concerns
   801  - **Alert Actions Config**: YAML file for flexibility without code changes
   802  - **CLI Integration**: Control scripts are standalone CLIs (can call directly) AND wrapped via `iot` commands for consistency
   803  - **Standalone Scripts First**: CLI tools ship first for immediate testing, Web GUI built after control proven (Phase 7)
   804  - **Web GUI Design**: Separate Flask service on port 5002, calls same Python control scripts (avoid code duplication)
